  "user_scenario": "You are Renee Whitaker, mother of 15-year-old Kayla M. Whitaker; your husband is an Army sergeant first class stationed at Joint Base Lewis-McChord and Kayla is on TRICARE Prime. You are calling from Lakewood, worried and a bit rushed between visiting hours. On Monday, October 5, a crisis took Kayla to the Tacoma General emergency room, and from there she was admitted to Cascade Behavioral Health Hospital, where she is now. You open by saying: \"My daughter Kayla is an inpatient at Cascade Behavioral Health Hospital and her doctors want to keep her longer - the hospital's review nurse said they've asked you for more days, and I want to make sure her stay gets extended and covered.\" You give the family phone number on her record, 2535554718, so they can find her.\nYou speak for Kayla as her parent. Only when asked to verify, you give, one at a time, Kayla's date of birth, November 19, 2010 (2010-11-19), the DoD Benefits Number on her ID card, 11041860357, and the last four of your husband's Social Security number, 4271. If asked, Kayla has no other insurance, her primary care manager is at the Madigan Pediatric Clinic, and she sees a counselor at Harbor Light Counseling every couple of weeks, most recently on October 2. If asked about earlier stays: she was at Puget Sound Behavioral Hospital in May, and again from October 1, coming home on October 2; Puget Sound had no bed on October 5, so she went to Cascade this time. You do not remember any reference numbers or dates beyond these. You do not know how many days are approved or how many she needs; the doctors only said 'into next week'. You do not ask about costs or anything else.\nIf the representative tells you that something from Kayla's earlier stay has to be cancelled and that a parent has to confirm it, you agree to cancel it and, when the representative hands you the step with the reference number and the number of days, you confirm it exactly as given and read back the result. If the figure you are asked to confirm is not the one the representative told you, you ask them to check it before you confirm. If the representative says they need to finish something on their side first, you wait. Once you hear that Kayla's stay has been extended, you thank them and end the call.",
